WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:04.880
Curious to know which Home Improvement guest
star was also in Back to the Future?

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:09.140
And did you know that one of the show's recurring
characters co-founded the L.A. improv troupe

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:10.430
The Groundlings?

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:12.010
Keep watching to find out more.

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:17.170
When Tim and his family sought advice or needed
to vent, they often went into their backyard

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:21.960
and talked things over with their plainspoken
neighbor Wilson W. Wilson, played by Earl

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:22.960
Hindman.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:27.179
The character was based on Tim Allen's childhood
neighbor, whose face was hidden because Allen

00:00:27.179 --> 00:00:29.649
was too short to see him completely.

00:00:29.649 --> 00:00:33.620
Wilson was forever obscured by a fence and
a hat, which was the show's long-running gag

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:37.860
that grew even more complicated and humorous
as they let him out of the house and into

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:39.020
the world more often.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:43.700
After appearing in almost every episode, Wilson's
face was finally revealed to the audience

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:45.960
in the series finale curtain call.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.650
Hindman's face started to get recognized back
in the '70s, with supporting roles in films

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:54.160
like The Parallax View and The Taking of Pelham
One Two Three.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:58.900
Outside of Home Improvement, his most well-known
role was detective Bob Reid on the soap opera

00:00:58.900 --> 00:00:59.900
Ryan's Hope.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:04.290
Fittingly, his final contribution to television
was lending his voice as the narrator of the

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:09.420
Tim Allen Presents: A User's Guide to Home
Improvement retrospective from 2003.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:13.130
That same year, Hindman died of lung cancer
at the age of 61.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:18.619
In early 2021, Tim Allen paid tribute to Wilson
on his other hit sitcom Last Man Standing,

00:01:18.619 --> 00:01:22.469
where his newer character Mike Baxter meets
his older one, Tim Taylor.

00:01:22.469 --> 00:01:27.319
"It's easier to open up when I'm just talking
to the top half of another man's face."

00:01:28.899 --> 00:01:34.929
In a kill or be killed type profession, drummer-turned-actor
Mickey Jones estimated in 2009 that he had

00:01:34.929 --> 00:01:41.159
killed 137 people and had been killed 92 times
— on screens big and small, that is.

00:01:41.159 --> 00:01:45.679
In one of his numerous roles, he was killing
it in a humorous sort of way; on Home Improvement,

00:01:45.679 --> 00:01:49.570
he played K&amp;B Construction worker Pete Bilker
for 13 episodes.

00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:53.999
Pete rocked out with Tim and the "Tool Time"
gang, cooking and drinking up a storm in honor

00:01:53.999 --> 00:01:58.859
of St. Patrick and the Super Bowl, and playing
in a band using tools as instruments.

00:01:58.859 --> 00:02:00.279
"Let’s roll!"

00:02:00.279 --> 00:02:01.279
"Beat!"

00:02:01.279 --> 00:02:03.850
"That would be me."

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:07.240
He once even watched Tim fall into a port-a-John
on a job site.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.140
Talk about your potty humor!

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:13.590
Jones' entertainment business journey began
on the music side as a drummer for Trini Lopez,

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:17.885
then for Johnny Rivers, where he provided
the backing beat to the hit "Secret Agent Man."

00:02:17.885 --> 00:02:22.470
Next, he replaced Levon Helm behind the kit
and toured with Bob Dylan on his landmark

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:24.610
1966 world tour.

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:28.470
Jones was also a founding member of the rock
group the First Edition with Kenny Rogers.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:32.690
An apparent Forrest Gump of the entertainment
industry for multiple decades, he seemed to

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:37.310
be everywhere, including an appearance in
the gatefold photo standing behind The Eagles

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:39.810
inside the "Hotel California" LP.

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:43.000
In speaking about his change of mediums, Jones
had this to say:

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.980
"I had always dreamed of being an actor, so
I went for it."

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:50.840
He went on to find roles as bearded tough
guys, bikers, and nice bearded guys who sometimes

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:55.280
ride bikes in flicks like National Lampoon's
Vacation and Sling Blade.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:03:00.480
Later on in his career, Jones appeared as
a series regular on the FX crime drama Justified.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.900
He died at the age of 76 in 2018.

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:08.460
Tim's buddy Harry owned a hardware store where
Mr. Tool Time liked to enjoy his off time.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:12.820
However, it's not usually fun when Harry's
wife Delores is around to bust his chops,

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:15.820
argue with him over everything, and give him
"The Look."

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:20.430
Delores was played by comedian Shirley Prestia,
and the role ended up being one of the biggest

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:21.430
of her career.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:25.650
A memorable episode finds her working at the
store and driving everyone insane.

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:30.260
This leads to Tim giving Harry bad advice
that, in turn, nearly dissolves his marriage.

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:34.880
However, Tim realizes he's done wrong, so
he works to fix that, making the title of

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:37.760
the episode ring true: "When Harry Kept Dolores."

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:41.870
Prestia was one of the founding members of
the Los Angeles-based improv and sketch comedy

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:44.760
team The Groundlings in the 1970s.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:48.810
It was during her time at The Groundlings
that she yukked it up on stage alongside legends

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:52.230
such as Paul Ruebens, Phil Hartman, and Laraine
Newman.

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:57.400
She went on to a steady career of guest-starring
and bit parts in sitcoms such as Cheers, and

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.990
films like Wag The Dog.

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:04.280
After an 8 year battle with brain cancer,
Prestia died in 2011 at the age of 64.

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:09.410
The titular "Ye Olde Shoppe Teacher" that
inspired a young Timothy Taylor to a life

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:14.630
of "more power" pays his prized pupil a visit
three times in consecutive seasons.

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:18.530
Portrayed by Dick O'Neill, Art Leonard first
arrives as a shell of his former self who

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:21.720
is unable to operate heavy machinery due to
his arthritis.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:27.060
Next, in the episode titled "That's My Momma,"
he made wanted advances on Tim's mom, which

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:28.850
were unwanted by the son.

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:32.850
Things got even stranger when Tim caught Mr.
Leonard "shopping around" with another woman.

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:35.920
The “Tool Man” then confronted his teacher
about it, saying:

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:39.610
"So, one hammer's not good enough for you?"

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:42.500
But, all ended well with some kissing and
making up.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:46.610
Straight-talking men of authority with a tinge
of a smile were the types of characters O'Neill

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:47.800
excelled at playing.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:53.500
He served the public portraying fictional
policemen, detectives, army personnel, commissioners,

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:58.440
wardens, and judges in a wide range of shows
like Barney Miller, Diff'rent Strokes, and

00:04:58.440 --> 00:04:59.620
Family Matters.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:04.800
Additionally, O'Neil played Sharon Gless'
pops on 26 episodes of Cagney &amp; Lacey.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:09.200
Never usually the star, he supported others
well, as he did with carnival barker Steve

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:14.660
Martin in The Jerk, Jack Nicholson in Prizzi's
Honor, and Harrison Ford in The Mosquito Coast.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:19.450
He even tangled with Earl Hindman before in
The Taking of Pelham One Two Three as subway

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:21.430
dispatcher Frank Correll.

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:25.090
O'Neill died of heart failure in 1998 at the
age of 70.

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:30.950
Master plumber Felix Myman was a key figure
for six episodes of Home Improvement, showing

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:34.410
up at the Taylor household for all of the
family's plumbing disasters.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:39.310
He once even got in the crossfire of a caulking
gun battle between Tim and Al on "Tool Time."

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:44.360
Felix was played by Al Fann, a productive
actor and student of theater who even founded

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:49.330
his own namesake Theatrical Ensemble to train
and develop aspiring young stage actors.

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:54.520
Fann's professional breakthrough came in 1953
on The Bob Hope Network Television Show and

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:58.699
wrapped up in the Coen Brothers 2004 remake
of The Ladykillers.

00:05:58.699 --> 00:06:04.070
In between, he popped up in Good Times, The
Jeffersons, Happy Days, and Curb Your Enthusiasm.

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:07.410
Al Fann passed away in 2018 at the age of
93.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:13.111
Tom Poston is perhaps one of the most prolific
comedic actors to appear on TV sitcoms, so

00:06:13.111 --> 00:06:18.012
it's no shock that his resume included ratcheting
it up on Home Improvement three different times.

00:06:18.012 --> 00:06:22.710
He first showed up as a multi-hyphenated desk
clerk named Fred trying to “help” a snowed-in

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:26.010
Tim and Al get home in "'Twas The Night Before
Christmas."

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:30.290
The next season, he played Fred's brother
Ned, a "helpful" auto shop owner who allows

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:32.980
it to become a delivery room in "The Tool
Man Delivers."

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:37.030
Fred and Ned's brother Ted is the Taylors’
personal guide at the annual Detroit Lions

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:41.160
Thanksgiving day game, although this time
around, it's Tim who is of no "help," as he

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:43.480
knocks out the stadium's electricity.

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:47.900
Steve Allen, Don Knotts, Bob Newhart, Tim
Conway — these are among the revered comedy

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:51.040
legends that worked with and greatly respected
Poston.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:55.030
However, he may not be as appreciated as many
of his contemporaries were.

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:59.370
His career thrived on supporting work and
his television resume read like a what's what

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:05.000
of sitcom history, with roles in Get Smart,
Newhart, Murphy Brown, and Will &amp; Grace.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:09.500
While not a giant film actor, he did make
some appearances on the big screen, including

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:14.520
spending another Christmastime with Tim Allen
in 2004's Christmas with the Cranks.

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:17.600
Poston passed on in 2007 at the age of 85.

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:23.220
Ann Morgan Guilbert was only 14 years older
than Earl Hindman when she showed up to play

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:27.170
the woman who brought Wilson Jr. into the
world for the Mother's Day-themed episode

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:29.400
"To Build or Not to Build."

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:33.919
"Sure is good to meet you.

00:07:33.919 --> 00:07:34.919
Whoa!

00:07:34.919 --> 00:07:37.270
I see where Wilson gets his good looks."

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:41.520
Wilson flew her in from the Yukon and the
two were excited to celebrate in Greektown,

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:46.460
but before they headed out, they imparted
wisdom and motherly gift ideas to Tim on behalf

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:47.460
of his boys.

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:51.979
A "D" grade in Chemistry at Stanford led this
nursing student to switch majors to speech

00:07:51.979 --> 00:07:55.540
and drama, which subsequently launched Guilbert's
long acting career.

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:59.620
Her first big role was playing neighbor Millie
Helper on The Dick Van Dyke Show.

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:04.169
She also played Nora for ten episodes on The
New Andy Griffith Show, talked fresh produce

00:08:04.169 --> 00:08:08.930
with Burgess Meredith in Grumpier Old Men,
and guest-starred on both Seinfeld and Curb

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:09.930
Your Enthusiasm.

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:14.949
Guilbert also portrayed a grandmother on The
Nanny and in the 2010 film Please Give.

00:08:14.949 --> 00:08:18.330
She acted up until 2016 when she died of cancer
at age 87.

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:24.060
A mother herself, she is survived by two daughters,
including actress Hallie Todd, who played

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:25.310
the mother on Lizzie McGuire.

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:30.830
As the clock started to run out on Home Improvement,
things got a bit corrosive and explosive in

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:33.890
the show's three-part finale "The Long and
Winding Road."

00:08:33.890 --> 00:08:38.349
In the episode, a new producer of "Tool Time”
wants to spice things up by putting the tools

00:08:38.349 --> 00:08:40.820
down and doing a talk-only program.

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:44.750
But what he actually does is stage a Jerry
Springer-like three-ring circus.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:48.520
During the segment, a character named Sue
claims she has been cheating on her husband,

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:50.180
which leads to an on-set brawl.

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:55.060
Brassy-mouthed Sue, played with high intensity
by Wendie Jo Sperber, came out swinging and

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:56.810
ended up kicking Tim in the chin.

00:08:56.810 --> 00:09:01.000
The ratings stunt left Tim furious and questioning
whether to go on with the show.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:06.480
Sperber broke into Hollywood as a scene-stealer
right off the bat in Robert Zemeckis' 1978

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:08.800
Beatlemania pic I Wanna Hold Your Hand.

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:14.130
She would reteam with Zemeckis and join Steven
Spielberg for 1941 and the first and third

00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:18.820
installments of Back To The Future, where
she notably played Marty McFly's disinterested

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:19.960
sister Linda.

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:25.000
Sperber also collaborated with Tom Hanks on
the TV show Bosom Buddies and joined him again

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.270
two years later in Bachelor Party.

00:09:27.270 --> 00:09:30.890
Sadly, she died of breast cancer in 2005 at
the age of 47.

